[node name="TitleText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="CanvasLayer/TitleScreen/MarginContainer" unique_id=2133776224]
layout_mode = 2
text = "Some things are older than memory itself.
They witnessed the rise and fall of entire civilizations and endured long after the people who once held them turned to dust.
History remembers great kings, the mighty heroes and events that shaped our world.
But history rarely remembers the things that were there all along.

You've always been curious about things others overlook.
This time it was just a stone.
You saw it at an auction. An unusual stone, smooth and strangely beautiful. 
There was something about it the made it hard to look away.
It wasn't expensive so you took it.
The stone sat in a glass case, carefully sealed away from curious hands. No markings. No known origin.

Just a stone...

On the way back the glass case slipped and shattered against the ground.
The stone rolled out onto the floor.
You picked it up with your bare hands...

The world disappeared.
No light. No sound. No ground. No stone.

Something beyond the darkness stirs.
Something that has waited far longer than you can imagine.
You are not alone here.

And then you see it...

"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false
horizontal_alignment = 1

